{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvoePWmvfHZW4zWryu3r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DKpPWDHbysrdZBQcXSKF5k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nplan={\n \"status\":\"ready\",\n \"central_topic\":\"Estimation error of regression-based global average treatment effect (GATE) estimators under network interference, characterized as corner-exposure extrapolation bias versus variance, across interference mechanisms, graphs and designs.\",\n \"core_methods\":[\n  \"regression-adjusted GATE estimation (fit outcome model on assigned treatments/neighbor exposures, predict all-treated vs all-control)\",\n  \"linear-in-neighbor-exposure ridge regression baseline and ridge ensembles with extrapolation-aware model selection\",\n  \"design-weighted (Horvitz-Thompson) residual correction / augmented regression\",\n  \"parametric exposure-mapping library with BIC-gated switch from linear fallback\",\n  \"block/wild bootstrap confidence intervals with design resampling\"],\n \"comparators\":[\n  \"difference-in-means (naive SUTVA) estimator\",\n  \"Horvitz-Thompson / Hajek estimators under exposure mappings (Aronow & Samii)\",\n  \"graph cluster randomization and network exposure (Ugander et al.; Eckles et al.)\",\n  \"model-based regression adjustment with graph-based covariates (Han & Ugander)\",\n  \"staggered rollout and covariance-optimized designs for total treatment effect\"],\n \"benchmarks\":[\n  \"synthetic networks (SBM, Barabasi-Albert, Watts-Strogatz) with synthetic interference outcomes\",\n  \"Facebook100 / socfb-Stanford3 and SNAP ego-Facebook public graphs only if used by the run\"],\n \"architectural_shifts\":[\n  \"flexible regression ensemble (worse than linear) -> linear base with shrunk design-weighted residual correction -> BIC-gated parametric exposure-mapping family with linear fallback\"],\n \"result_driven_themes\":[\n  \"extrapolation to the all-treated/all-control corner makes bias dominate error (bias_rel ~0.16-0.19 vs rmse ~0.18-0.23) for flexible models\",\n  \"correctly specified exposure functional form reduces error in nonlinear-interference cases (case 6: 0.71 -> 0.27) while some cases remain unresolved (case 8 ~0.45)\",\n  \"bootstrap CI undercoverage (0.67-0.81) under misspecification\",\n  \"model selection by information criterion for exposure-response specification\"],\n \"queries\":[\n  {\"query\":\"regression adjustment global average treatment effect network interference\",\"category\":\"core_method\",\"rationale\":\"Central estimator family (Chin 2019 and follow-ups); needed to position the extrapolation-error characterization.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"model-based regression adjustment network interference graph covariates bootstrap confidence intervals\",\"category\":\"core_method\",\"rationale\":\"Closest method family (Han & Ugander) and source of block-bootstrap inference comparable to our design-resampling bootstrap.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"exposure mapping misspecification bias network interference total treatment effect estimation\",\"category\":\"result_driven_theme\",\"rationale\":\"Run shows bias dominates when the functional form of interference is wrong; need literature on misspecified exposure mappings.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"Horvitz-Thompson Hajek estimator general interference exposure probability variance\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"HT and Hajek baselines were run; Aronow & Samii and variance-bound work are expected comparators.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"graph cluster randomization network exposure bias variance tradeoff\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Design-side comparator for reducing interference bias; relevant to the design axis of the simulation.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"difference-in-means bias under interference randomized experiments SUTVA violation\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Naive difference-in-means baseline had rmse_rel ~0.62 versus 0.14-0.18 for regression estimators.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"augmented inverse probability weighting doubly robust residual correction interference network\",\"category\":\"architectural_shift\",\"rationale\":\"Second variant adds design-weighted residual correction to a linear base, an AIPW/doubly-robust-style construction.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"staggered rollout design total treatment effect interference without network knowledge\",\"category\":\"baseline_comparator\",\"rationale\":\"Alternative design/estimator family for GATE under low-order interference, named in starter literature.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"extrapolation all-treated all-control counterfactual positivity violation network exposure\",\"category\":\"result_driven_theme\",\"rationale\":\"Central finding: error governed by extrapolation to rarely observed full-exposure corner under random designs.\"},\n  {\"query\":\"Facebook100 social structure of Facebook networks\",\"category\":\"benchmark_context\",\"rationale\":\"Public graph data context if Facebook100 graphs were used for evaluation; cite data provenance only.\"}],\n \"forbidden_query_patterns\":[\n  \"generic optimization / benchmarking / scientific method / AI scientist phrasing\",\n  \"campaign order, iteration, milestone or search-history phrasing\",\n  \"graph neural network / spectral convolution queries (starter-list GCN papers are not supported by the run's methods)\",\n  \"any query targeting the specific published paper on this research question, its title, authors, or results\",\n  \"internal harness terms (combined_score, rubric, eligible, worker)\"],\n \"failure_reason\":\"\"}\njson.dump(plan,open('reference_query_plan.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nmd=\"\"\"# Reference Query Plan\n\n**Central topic.** Estimation error of regression-based GATE estimators under network interference, framed as corner-exposure extrapolation bias versus variance across interference mechanisms, graphs and designs.\n\n## Grounding\nThree model variants were run: (1) a flexible ridge regression ensemble with extrapolation-aware selection (relative RMSE 0.232, worse than the linear baseline 0.184); (2) a linear base with shrunk design-weighted residual correction (0.185); (3) a BIC-gated parametric exposure-mapping library with linear fallback (0.140, bias 0.092, CI coverage 0.81). Baselines run: difference-in-means (0.62), Horvitz-Thompson (0.92), linear regression (0.18), oracle (0.05). Case 6 improved from about 0.71 to 0.27 with the parametric family; case 8 stays at about 0.45.\n\n## Core methods\nRegression-adjusted GATE; linear ridge baseline; design-weighted residual correction; BIC-gated parametric exposure mappings; design-resampling block/wild bootstrap.\n\n## Comparators\nDifference-in-means; HT/Hajek exposure estimators; graph cluster randomization; Han & Ugander regression adjustment; staggered rollout.\n\n## Benchmarks\nSynthetic SBM/BA/WS graphs; Facebook100 (Stanford3) and SNAP ego-Facebook only if used.\n\n## Queries (10)\n1. regression adjustment global average treatment effect network interference (core_method)\n2. model-based regression adjustment network interference graph covariates bootstrap confidence intervals (core_method)\n3. exposure mapping misspecification bias network interference total treatment effect estimation (result_driven_theme)\n4. Horvitz-Thompson Hajek estimator general interference exposure probability variance (baseline_comparator)\n5. graph cluster randomization network exposure bias variance tradeoff (baseline_comparator)\n6. difference-in-means bias under interference randomized experiments SUTVA violation (baseline_comparator)\n7. augmented inverse probability weighting doubly robust residual correction interference network (architectural_shift)\n8. staggered rollout design total treatment effect interference without network knowledge (baseline_comparator)\n9. extrapolation all-treated all-control counterfactual positivity violation network exposure (result_driven_theme)\n10. Facebook100 social structure of Facebook networks (benchmark_context)\n\n## Rejected alternatives\nGeneric queries (optimization, benchmarking, AI-scientist, chronology of attempts) and GCN/spectral-convolution queries were rejected: the run's methods contain no graph neural networks, so those starter-list papers are not supported by results. No query targets the excluded published paper.\n\"\"\"\nopen('reference_query_plan.md','w').write(md)\nnote=\"\\n### 2026-11-11 | step=reference_plan\\n- Wrote reference_query_plan.{md,json}: 10 queries on regression GATE, exposure-mapping misspecification, HT/Hajek, cluster randomization, DiM, AIPW-style correction, staggered rollout, extrapolation/positivity, Facebook100. Rejected generic process queries and GCN/spectral queries (no GNN in run). Avoids excluded paper.\\n\"\nfor p in ['memory.md','global_memory/memory.md']:\n    open(p,'a').write(note)\nopen('global_memory/memory.jsonl','a').write(json.dumps({\"step\":\"reference_plan\",\"scope\":\"planning\",\"summary\":\"10-query plan grounded in regression-GATE, exposure mapping, HT/Hajek, cluster randomization, DiM, AIPW-style, staggered rollout; rejected generic and GCN queries.\"})+\"\\n\")\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3627,"cache_read_input_tokens":30094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3627},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f712d45-8a52-4b42-9156-4718f17abdee","uuid":"d51064f9-c245-4796-8f92-e772b86ec6d1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:13:24.259Z","request_id":"req_011CgvoePFQ5U8ywAv6NctRM"}
